# routes-enabled — the CONSENT half of the registry (ai-template's enable-list).
#
# agents.registry.csv is a CATALOG. This file is the ordered list of route ids
# a caller may actually name. An absent or empty file is "no routes", and the
# service refuses to start rather than treating that as "everything" — an empty
# pool is a consent decision, not a broken file.
#
# One id per line, `#` comments. Adding a line is the whole of turning a route
# on; nothing else has to change.

# The default, and A40's own finding is that it is the right default: song
# grouping and categorisation are classification work, which wants an answer
# rather than an agent, so the cheapest row leads.
ANALYSIS-QUICK

# Deeper analysis. Uncomment when a consumer needs it — the subscription is one
# pool and this row competes with the interactive quota.
# ANALYSIS-DEEP

# The second family. Off until a consumer needs cross-family diversity; it also
# needs the codex CLI carried and signed in on the same dedicated account.
# ANALYSIS-CODEX
